# frame-ancestors is 'self', not 'none': the ebook reader runs foliate-js in a
# same-origin iframe (/reader/index.html), and 'none' blocks a page from being
# framed even by its own origin - the reader failed with "Framing
# 'https://app.dosya.dev/' violates ... frame-ancestors 'none'". 'self' still
# refuses every third-party frame, which is the clickjacking threat this
# directive exists for; it only stops the site refusing itself.
# connect-src lists the two R2 S3 hostnames (main account + the EU
# jurisdiction bucket) because the Vault fetches presigned chunk PUT/GET URLs
# against them directly from the browser. Explicit hosts on purpose: a
# *.r2.cloudflarestorage.com wildcard would let an injected script exfiltrate
# to any R2 account. Keep in step with apps/api/src/lib/r2-buckets.ts.
# Cloudflare Web Analytics is auto-injected at the edge for this zone, so
# script-src allows static.cloudflareinsights.com (the beacon) and connect-src
# allows cloudflareinsights.com (its /cdn-cgi/rum POST), per Cloudflare's CSP
# guidance. Not allowed on purpose: the inline bot JavaScript-detections
# snippet Cloudflare also injects; it needs a per-request nonce, which a
# static headers file cannot mint, and 'unsafe-inline' would gut script-src.
# get.microsoft.com is in four directives for one component: the official
# <ms-store-badge> in the "Get the apps" row on /checkout/success
# (src/components/ms-store-badge.tsx). It loads its script from there
# (script-src), draws its artwork from get.microsoft.com/images (img-src),
# always appends a 0x0 iframe to get.microsoft.com/iframe.html (frame-src), and
# in window-mode="direct" fetches the Windows installer (connect-src). Miss one
# and the badge silently does not render. Keep in step with the same four
# entries in the marketing site's public/_headers.
# connect-src also names the Sentry ingest host (src/lib/sentry.ts): crash
# reports are a POST from the browser, and without it every report would be
# refused at the CSP while the app kept telling users "We've been notified".
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://docs.dosya.dev https://get.microsoft.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' blob:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://api.dosya.dev https://get.microsoft.com; media-src 'self' blob: data: https://api.dosya.dev; font-src 'self' blob: data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.dosya.dev https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://docs.dosya.dev https://get.microsoft.com https://0b25394b353c95a526538e19706809e8.r2.cloudflarestorage.com https://0b25394b353c95a526538e19706809e8.eu.r2.cloudflarestorage.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://o4512130123825152.ingest.de.sentry.io; frame-src 'self' blob: https://api.dosya.dev https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://docs.dosya.dev https://get.microsoft.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

# Vite content-hashes everything under /assets/, so cache forever. Unhashed
# files (theme-init.js, sw.js, favicons) keep the Pages default revalidation.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
